# Row B2: settlement representation (x/apibench/b2). See hack/bakeoff.sh.
PKG=./x/apibench/b2
BENCH=BenchmarkAPI/Settlement
REF=token
AUTO_KEY=b2
# the benchmark configuration: this row is one of the MUTUALLY EXCLUSIVE API shapes.
# Only one shape can be the API, so a shape the API did not take is a loser
# in §9.4(5)'s sense and cannot be retained as a profile the way a §9.1 arm
# can.
CLASS=B
#
# `git worktree add <path> d802b9e4e8c9` restores every shape this row
# measured, which is what makes a re-ratification on a pinned host still
# possible.
REMOVED=retired
ADR=5
TITLE="Settlement representation: packed token, per-delivery closure, settlement object (B2)"
# The micro benchmark runs in the reuse ownership mode, where the broker
# allocates nothing, so allocs/op is what the representation itself costs: the
# closure representation allocates one closure per delivery by construction and
# the other two reach zero. BenchmarkAPIBench/B1/<shape>/settle=<kind> measures
# the same three representations inside a whole delivery round.
# The row has no line counts of its own: the settlement representation is
# invisible in a caller's code — a delivery is acknowledged with d.Ack()
# whichever handle it carries — so its DX evidence is the misuse column of
# x/apibench/b1's TestMisuse (run once per representation) and the allocation
# numbers, not the five developer tasks.

#
# CRITERION is the benchmark configuration's decision column for this row, quoted.
# MATRIX is the IQMQ_BENCH_MATRIX grid the campaign measures the family at.
# DECIDED_AT names the benchmark-name segments the criterion is read at, and
# DECIDED_ON the metrics; `make bench-lint` lists the family's benchmarks at
# the declared grid and fails when a term or a metric is missing from the rows
# every kind has in common, which is the only data `bakeoff decide` reads.
CRITERION="Settler + token (allocs per delivery; Kafka offset-style and SQS receipt-style workloads; race stress)"
# MATRIX=default is the only grid: x/apibench/b2 has no IQMQ_BENCH_MATRIX
# branch.
MATRIX=default
DECIDED_AT="Settlement"
DECIDED_ON="allocs/op ns/settle"
# This family is decided from ONE row per kind -- `BenchmarkAPI/Settlement/
# <kind>`, a claim, a settle and a recycle over 256 deliveries -- which is
# enough for the criterion's metric (allocations per delivery) and is all the
# comparable set there is: after the kind segment is stripped, the three kinds
# share the single name `BenchmarkAPI/Settlement`. The two driver-shaped
# workloads §9.2 names beside it (Kafka offset-style, SQS receipt-style) are
# not dimensions of this benchmark and are measured nowhere; the Kafka
# offset-style ack lives in family A14's own root. Assumption A24.70.
